""============================================================================
"" The file types below were added to this tree; everything above came with
"" JVim 3.0-j2.1b. Two things to know before adding more:
""
""   o A rule is one search, and the leftmost match on the line wins; where two
""     rules start at the same column the earlier one wins. So comments and
""     strings go at the top of a block, and a narrower rule goes before the
""     wider one it would otherwise lose to.
""   o ":syntax" is an ex command, so "|" separates commands and '"' starts a
""     comment before the rule is ever seen. Write '"' as \" -- the backslash
""     is eaten on the way in, which is what the existing rules above do. \|
""     cannot be rescued the same way: there is no alternation in a rule.
""============================================================================
